> A hand-checkable calculation

Reward1, discount.9 and next action values2,4 give target4.6. A half-step update from zero gives2.3, regardless of which next action was sampled.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/q_learning_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace f=dm::rl::foundations;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");f::QTable q(2,2);q(1,0)=2;q(1,1)=4;float target=1+.9f*q.Max(1);q(0,0)+=.5f*(target-q(0,0));std::vector<double>values{target,q(0,0)};if(std::abs(q(0,0)-2.3f)>1e-6)return 1;std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/q_learning_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"worked values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("q learning worked calculation").x_label("Displayed coordinate").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/q_learning_worked.svg");}
